In particular, all graphs we consider will be bipartite, and the transducer will be a product of reflections: one around the spaces corresponding to the first part of the bipartition, and another around the spaces corresponding to the other part of the bipartition. Note that some edges have only one endpoint. We call these boundary edges.}\label{fig:aa-transducer}
